{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A narrow pattern with a striking payoff. It applies when an array holds numbers from a **known, contiguous range** — typically 1 to N, or 0 to N−1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Under that condition, problems that look like they need a hash set can be solved in **O(N) time with O(1) space**."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The observation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If an array holds exactly the numbers 0 to N−1, there is only one sorted arrangement, and in it **every value sits at the index equal to itself**. Value 0 at index 0, value 3 at index 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "So each value already knows where it belongs. No comparisons needed — just put it there."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/54164504-b000-4b61-85b6-a0fb4f1345c9.svg",
      "alt": "Each value being swapped into the slot matching its own number",
      "caption": "Value 3 belongs at index 3 — keep swapping until every value is home",
      "width": 900,
      "height": 280,
